IDEAS

This folder keeps the ideas we find in other projects: what they do
well that this repository's project should learn from, and what they do
badly that it should avoid.


ONE FILE PER PROJECT

  <name>.md, for example hyprland.md or bash.md. Each file has:

    What it is           language, license, size, scope
    Ideas worth taking   each with a verdict and a reason
    Things to avoid      each with a reason
    Where to look        files or docs to read when we act on an idea

  Verdicts:

    adopt     we want this; it has (or will get) a place in a plan
    consider  promising; needs a closer look or Fred's view
    reject    we decided against it, and the reason says why

  An idea that the project builds gets the plan or version that
  delivered it, for example "adopt (P1, 0.0.4)". When code is taken, not
  just the idea, it is also recorded in UPSTREAM.md and COPYRIGHT.

  A synthesis.md, where there is one, gathers the best ideas from every
  file by topic, and is the place to start.


REFERENCE CLONES

  sources lists the projects we keep a local clone of, so we can read
  their code and follow their fixes. tools/pull-references brings every
  listed clone up to date and clones any that are missing:

    tools/pull-references          pull every listed clone
    tools/pull-references --list   show what is listed and where

  The clones live outside this repository (under ~/Code). Nothing is
  ever pushed or posted to those projects.


HOW DEEP THESE NOTES GO

  Notes say whether they come from reading the project's source or are
  starter notes from its known design. Starter notes are checked against
  the source before we act on them. A full "survey the field" happens
  only when Fred asks for one.


IN THIS REPOSITORY

  Start with synthesis.md. It gathers the best ideas from 29 surveyed
  projects and tools by topic and names five useful first moves.
  Every verdict in these files is a research judgment, not an approved
  plan or version. No code or expressive text was taken, so UPSTREAM.md
  and COPYRIGHT are unchanged.

